            <profile id="2e49-a079-d49a-7fce" name="Equipment and options (as printed in WAB2 army list)" publicationId="15ea-5299-d0f5-5dbb" hidden="false" typeId="b19e-ee0c-17d1-6e33" typeName="Equipment and Notes">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Text" typeId="63ac-8f60-d28a-2232">Hand weapon and light armour. May either have throwing or thrusting spear (+2 pts) and shield (+2 pts), or, if mounted, kontos (+3 pts) and buckler (+1 pt). May exchange light armour for heavy armour (+1 pt). May ride a horse (free) or warhorse (+8 pts), which may be barded (+4 pts). Characters on foot may be Riding Horses (+1 pt). Gepid or Lombard characters may take Kontarion &amp; shield (+4 pts). One Noble or Great Noble model may be upgraded to War Banner Bearer (+15 pts); the War Banner Bearer may not take a spear or kontos and is the Army Standard Bearer. Nobles were known as duces and comites. (Byzantium p.53)</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
            <profile id="d9ea-3e93-26c2-0862" name="Armour Save" hidden="false" typeId="0dbe-f4ed-ef08-8e86" typeName="Armour Save">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Save" typeId="603e-2898-6af9-6cf1">6+</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="With conditional bonuses" typeId="5882-dd5a-bc28-4024">-</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="Notes" typeId="d5e4-804e-6192-0114">Armour save from armour, shield and barding bonus pips (rulebook pp.95-98); maximum 3+ (2+ for barded cavalry). M already includes encumbrance for armour/barding (p.96). Conditional pips are in the next column.</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
              <modifiers>
                <!-- armour-save -->
