            </profile>
            <profile id="aa4e-e3f9-704d-1361" name="Equipment and options (as printed in WAB2 army list)" publicationId="15ea-5299-d0f5-5dbb" hidden="false" typeId="b19e-ee0c-17d1-6e33" typeName="Equipment and Notes">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Text" typeId="63ac-8f60-d28a-2232">Hand weapon, throwing or thrusting spear, light armour and shield. May either have javelins (+1 pt), or exchange spear &amp; shield for kontos (+1 pt), and take buckler (+1 pt). May have heavy armour instead of light armour (+1 pt). Warriors on foot may be Riding Horses (+1 pt). Mounted Warriors are Superior Germanic Cavalry. Combined Units - Warriors may combine with Freemen. For every Warrior model in the army, at least two Freeman models must be taken as well (not enforced).  (Byzantium p.54)</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
            <profile id="f1e0-80de-a51a-8aad" name="Armour Save" hidden="false" typeId="0dbe-f4ed-ef08-8e86" typeName="Armour Save">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Save" typeId="603e-2898-6af9-6cf1">5+</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="With conditional bonuses" typeId="5882-dd5a-bc28-4024">-</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="Notes" typeId="d5e4-804e-6192-0114">Armour save from armour, shield and barding bonus pips (rulebook pp.95-98); maximum 3+ (2+ for barded cavalry). M already includes encumbrance for armour/barding (p.96). Conditional pips are in the next column.</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
              <modifiers>
