  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="8972-7728-4075-2727" name="Germanic Kingdoms (Byzantium) - List Notes" publicationId="15ea-5299-d0f5-5dbb" hidden="false">
      <description>GERMANIC KINGDOMS (Byzantium: Beyond the Golden Gate, pp.50-54): Vandals, Visigoths, Ostrogoths, Franks, Gepids and Lombards, 442-800 AD. All Mounted Comitatus, Warriors and Freemen count against the Cavalry percentage; all other troops count against the Infantry percentage. COMBINED UNITS: Warrior Elite may combine with 50-75% Freemen, who are placed in the rear ranks. As long as at least half of the models in the first rank are Warrior Elite, the Save and Leadership value of the Warriors is used. Half of all missile hits inflicted on a combined unit count as being inflicted on the Warriors. In close combat, enemy models in base contact with Warriors must fight against them. If excess casualties are inflicted these "carry over" to the Freemen. The last Warriors removed are the Leader, Musician and Standard. Some Germanic armies are allowed to field combined units in skirmish formation: use the Leadership value of the Warriors if at least half of the models in the skirmishing unit are Warrior models; when shooting at a Combined Unit in skirmish formation use the save of the majority of the models (the better save if equal). Combined units are not built as mixed units: take Warriors and Freemen as separate unit entries and combine them on the table.

ARMY COMPOSITIONS (pick one in the Army composition list):
[Germanic Kingdoms - African Vandal Kingdom]
  Characters: up to 25%
  Cavalry: at least 50%
  Infantry: up to 20%
  AFRICAN VANDAL KINGDOM (442-535 AD). Characters up to 25%; Cavalry at least 50%; Infantry up to 20%. Allies: two units of Berber Light Cavalry. All Vandal Cavalry count as Light Cavalry and have Feigned Flight (+1 pt). Vandal Freemen Cavalry must have a hand weapon and throwing or thrusting spears instead of mixed weapons (+1 pt). Vandal Comitatus and Warrior Cavalry may not take javelins.
[Germanic Kingdoms - Gallic and Spanish Visigoths]
  Characters: up to 25%
  Cavalry: up to 66%
  Infantry: up to 33%
  GALLIC &amp; SPANISH VISIGOTHS (475-720 AD). Characters up to 25%; Cavalry up to 66%; Infantry up to 33%. To represent Basque Light Cavalry two Freemen Cavalry units may have Leadership 7 (+1 pt) - they may take no further equipment.
[Germanic Kingdoms - Early Merovingian Franks]
  Characters: up to 25%
  Cavalry: up to 25%
  Infantry: at least 50%
  EARLY MEROVINGIAN FRANKS (c.450-561 AD). Characters up to 25%; Cavalry up to 25%; Infantry at least 50%. Frankish Comitatus and Warrior units on foot may take heavy throwing spears instead of throwing or thrusting spear (+2 pts; fransisca/angon). Infantry units not armed with fransisca axes count as Levies. Two such units may use a shieldwall formation (+1 pt). Merovingian Frankish Warrior Cavalry may not take thrusting spear or kontos &amp; buckler.
[Germanic Kingdoms - Italian Ostrogoths]
  Characters: up to 25%
  Cavalry: up to 66%
  Infantry: up to 50%
  ITALIAN OSTROGOTHS (493-561 AD). Characters up to 25%; Cavalry up to 66%; Infantry up to 50%. Allies: two units of either Foederati Heavy Cavalry or Berber Light Cavalry. The Ostrogothic Comitatus and one unit of Warrior Cavalry may take barding for their mounts (+4 pts).
[Germanic Kingdoms - Gepids and Early Lombards]
  Characters: up to 25%
  Cavalry: up to 66%
  Infantry: up to 33%
  GEPIDS &amp; EARLY LOMBARDS (451-567 AD / 800 AD). Characters up to 25%; Cavalry up to 66%; Infantry up to 33%. Gepid or Lombard characters may take Kontarion &amp; shield (+4 pts). Comitatus and Warrior Cavalrymen must either take kontos or Kontarion (+1 pt) instead of spear. Gepid or Lombard Freemen on foot count as Light Infantry, Leadership 6 and cost 6 points each. Two units of Freemen on foot may exchange javelins for heavy throwing spears (+3 pts) to represent Saxons: allies, not Light Infantry, Warband Psychology rules 1 &amp; 2.</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
</catalogue>
